+## Dispatch interval boundaries (#1216)
+
+Adjacent blocks share intervals only when there is a CFG edge from the earlier
+block to the later one. The existing phi, liveness and fixed-range boundary
+checks still apply. Alternative dispatch handlers get independent ranges, so
+register pressure in one cannot become a sibling's incoming spill state merely
+through layout order. Real layout edges retain coalescing across branches and
+joins; ordinary edge moves carry values between the independent ranges.
+
+`test-tier1-cfg` covers dispatch handlers with local pressure and clobbers,
+back edges and retained merging on real branch and chain edges, through both allocator
+paths and the existing verifier and certificate oracles. These fixtures check
+allocation behavior; the issue's dynamic speedtest1/five-script edge-traffic
+target and 9700X runtime requirement still need workload measurements.
+
 ## Edge validation and emission indexing (#1356)
 
 `tier1_cfg_input_valid` checks both complete offset arrays before any edge-array
